From: pilali
Subject: [PATCH] NAM Core: undef glibc's major/minor macros before nam::Version

glibc's <sys/types.h> (pulled in transitively by <fstream>, <memory>, etc.)
defines major() and minor() as macros that expand to gnu_dev_major /
gnu_dev_minor. They collide with the homonymous data members of
nam::Version, so the preprocessor rewrites the constructor's initialiser
list to gnu_dev_major(major) and the build fails with:

    error: class 'nam::Version' does not have any field named 'gnu_dev_major'

glibc 2.28+ gates these macros behind _DEFAULT_SOURCE, but moddwarf-new's
sysroot ships glibc 2.27, where they're still leaked unconditionally.

Undef them locally in get_dsp.h, after the headers that pull <sys/types.h>
in transitively. No-op on systems where the macros aren't defined.

--- a/deps/NeuralAudio/deps/NeuralAmpModelerCore/NAM/get_dsp.h
+++ b/deps/NeuralAudio/deps/NeuralAmpModelerCore/NAM/get_dsp.h
@@ -6,6 +6,13 @@

 #include "dsp.h"

+// glibc's <sys/types.h> (pulled in transitively by <fstream>, <memory>, …)
+// exposes major()/minor() as macros on glibc < 2.28 (moddwarf-new's sysroot
+// ships glibc 2.27). They shadow the Version members below — the
+// preprocessor would rewrite them to gnu_dev_major / gnu_dev_minor.
+#undef major
+#undef minor
+
 namespace nam
 {
 enum class Supported
